    "updated_at": "2019-10-09T23:53:02Z",
    "body": "@rniwa Web-compat here is an interesting question... the default of generating an inline box is useless: borders don't go around the image, and the margin only has an effect in the inline axis. Anyone styling that box would need to convert it to a block or inline-block first. And any such explicit `display` declaration would override one in the style sheet, so there would be no Web-compat concern there. But there are some other properties in CSS that convert inlines to blocks as a side-effect--if an author is using those and relying on that side-effect rather than setting `display: block` explicitly, then we'd have a problem.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
